.IX Title "Clownfish::Vector 3pm"
.TH Clownfish::Vector 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Clownfish::Vector \- Variable\-sized array.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 3
\&    my $vector = Clownfish::Vector\->new;
\&    $vector\->store($tick, $value);
\&    my $value = $vector\->fetch($tick);
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 3
\&    my $vector = Clownfish::Vector\->new(
\&        capacity => $capacity,  # default: 0
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Return a new Vector.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBcapacity\fR \- Initial number of elements that the object will be able
to hold before reallocation.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS push
.IX Subsection "push"
.Vb 2
\&    $vector\->push($element);
\&    $vector\->push();  # default: undef
.Ve
.PP
Push an item onto the end of a Vector.
.SS push_all
.IX Subsection "push_all"
.Vb 1
\&    $vector\->push_all($other);
.Ve
.PP
Push all the elements of another Vector onto the end of this one.
.SS pop
.IX Subsection "pop"
.Vb 1
\&    my $obj = $vector\->pop();
.Ve
.PP
Pop an item off of the end of a Vector.
.PP
Returns: the element or undef if the Vector is empty.
.SS insert
.IX Subsection "insert"
.Vb 4
\&    $vector\->insert(
\&        tick    => $tick,     # required
\&        element => $element,  # default: undef
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Insert an element at \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR moving the following elements.
.SS insert_all
.IX Subsection "insert_all"
.Vb 4
\&    $vector\->insert_all(
\&        tick  => $tick,   # required
\&        other => $other,  # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Inserts elements from \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR vector at \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR moving the following
elements.
.SS fetch
.IX Subsection "fetch"
.Vb 1
\&    my $obj = $vector\->fetch($tick);
.Ve
.PP
Fetch the element at \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR.
.PP
Returns: the element or undef if \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR is out of bounds.
.SS store
.IX Subsection "store"
.Vb 1
\&    $vector\->store($tick, $elem)
.Ve
.PP
Store an element at index \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR, possibly displacing an existing element.
.SS delete
.IX Subsection "delete"
.Vb 1
\&    my $obj = $vector\->delete($tick);
.Ve
.PP
Replace an element in the Vector with undef and return it.
.PP
Returns: the element stored at \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR or undef if \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR is out of
bounds.
.SS excise
.IX Subsection "excise"
.Vb 4
\&    $vector\->excise(
\&        offset => $offset,  # required
\&        length => $length,  # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Remove \f(CW\*(C`length\*(C'\fR elements from the Vector, starting at \f(CW\*(C`offset\*(C'\fR.
Move elements over to fill in the gap.
.SS clone
.IX Subsection "clone"
.Vb 1
\&    my $arrayref = $vector\->clone();
.Ve
.PP
Clone the Vector but merely increment the refcounts of its elements
rather than clone them.
.SS sort
.IX Subsection "sort"
.Vb 1
\&    $vector\->sort();
.Ve
.PP
Sort the Vector.  Sort order is guaranteed to be \fIstable\fR: the
relative order of elements which compare as equal will not change.
.SS resize
.IX Subsection "resize"
.Vb 1
\&    $vector\->resize($size);
.Ve
.PP
Set the size for the Vector.  If the new size is larger than the
current size, grow the object to accommodate undef elements; if
smaller than the current size, decrement and discard truncated elements.
.SS clear
.IX Subsection "clear"
.Vb 1
\&    $vector\->clear();
.Ve
.PP
Empty the Vector.
.SS get_size
.IX Subsection "get_size"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $vector\->get_size();
.Ve
.PP
Return the size of the Vector.
.SS slice
.IX Subsection "slice"
.Vb 4
\&    my $arrayref = $vector\->slice(
\&        offset => $offset,  # required
\&        length => $length,  # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Return a slice of the Vector consisting of elements from a contiguous
range.  If the specified range is out of bounds, return a slice with
fewer elements – potentially none.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBoffset\fR \- The index of the element to start at.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBlength\fR \- The maximum number of elements to slice.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Clownfish::Vector isa Clownfish::Obj.
